Change(genesis='66602cd0dec37d58d03eec9518ca805a7ac38ea912d2b0c366a0b67b4b9f50b6', deps=('03bda2e09397e6414bcec003c67b91d5612724806f61537ab67d1727eb65e3bb',), event=Revised(decision='twochains', at=datetime(2026, 11, 20, 0, 0, 0), actor='assistant', title="An instance's chains are ordered, the first the owner's todos; the roadmap and the upkeep chain are named by role", body="*An instance holds as many chains as its `[[chains]]` declares, in order* (`suzatary_base::chains`). The ORDER means one thing: the first chain is what a verb with no `--chain`, the bare `/api/…` paths and the briefing read, and on this deployment it is `life`, the owner's own todos. Two chains are named by role, never by their place in the order. *The roadmap* is the one chain whose store holds a `releases.toml` beside it (`versionreading`): a public store, written only by the owner and the main session (`publictaskwords`), published by the next hourly pass behind door 2 (`scripts/safe-push.sh`), and read for the version. *Upkeep* is the chain `[upkeep] chain` names: the system's private work, where every automated filer writes (`failuresaretodos`); an instance that names none files nothing. *The routing rule*, as OPERATOR.md, SECRETARY.md and the triage prompt state it, naming the chain as `context`'s `authoring.upkeep_chain`: anything about the SYSTEM (a failing gate, a flaky test, a broken sync, a verb to fix) goes to the upkeep chain; anything about THE OWNER'S LIFE goes to `life`. A task for the public roadmap is written deliberately (`roadmappinscode`), never routed there. A todo cannot move between chains. The trust policy and actor roster belong to a chain (`suzatary_base::chains::ChainPolicy`); the tailnet door, the categories and the app URL are the deployment's. Routes take the chain as a path segment (`/api/<chain>/…`); mail, briefings and device registration are not scoped.", rationale="Decided 2026-09-09 (ARCHITECTURE §10.2). Restated 2026-11-20: the project's public tasks moved to the roadmap store on 2026-11-17, and the system's own work to the chain `[upkeep]` names.", supersedes=()))